    "result_text": "All 268 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the sequential membership number feature for newly created owners:\n\n1. **OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` integer (int32) property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field at build time.\n\n2. **Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field mapped to a new `membership_number` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it to/from `OwnerDto` by name (no mapper change needed).\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Tests use the `hsqldb` schema with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL change is what makes the value persist and be readable via `GET`.\n\n4. **New pipeline step** (`function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`) \u2014 reads the current owner count and assigns `count + 1` to the owner, running under the transaction governance before the save step.\n\n5. **POST pipeline wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignMembershipNumber` step between `checkDuplicate` and `save`, so the count reflects only pre-existing owners and duplicates/validation failures don't consume a number.\n\nThe `Cp09Tests` acceptance test (two consecutive creations differ by exactly one) passes, as does the full suite. The value is assigned before save, and because Hibernate auto-flushes before the `findAll()` query, the second creation within a transaction correctly sees the first, yielding a strictly incrementing sequence.",
